    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "```suggestion\r\nexport type TransformItems<\r\n  TItem,\r\n  TMetaData = {\r\n    results?: SearchResults;\r\n  }\r\n> = (items: TItem[], metadata: TMetadata) => TItem[];\r\n```\r\n\r\nwe shouldn't link item to results, as item is only the hits inside the hits/infinitehits component, where you can pass the generic explicitly by overriding TMetadata. What do you think?",
    "commit_id": "f9597f587d71cef0bd6089a6517e0da38abdaa68",
    "created_at": "2022-01-27T13:44:38Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -270,7 +270,12 @@ export type Widget<\n /**\n  * Transforms the given items.\n  */\n-export type TransformItems<TItem> = (items: TItem[]) => TItem[];\n+export type TransformItems<TItem, TResults = SearchResults<TItem>> = (\n+  items: TItem[],\n+  metadata: {\n+    results: TResults | undefined;\n+  }\n+) => TItem[];",
